     "gills",
     "excretion"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Respiration is the process by which cells use oxygen to release energy from food and give out carbon dioxide. We breathe in oxygen through the nose, which reaches the lungs.\nDifferent animals breathe differently: fish use gills, insects use tiny holes called spiracles and earthworms breathe through the skin.\nExcretion removes waste. Humans remove waste through kidneys (urine), skin (sweat) and lungs (carbon dioxide)."
    }
